  "description": "PF7 backward with only two records above the anchor - a short backward page, and the one case that takes NEITHER page-number arm. CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST arrives as ADMIN003, so over the ten records of app/jcl/DUSRSECJ.jcl exactly two records precede the anchor, and :248 pages backward because the count is 2. :342-343 discards the anchor itself, :346-350 blanks all ten rows to SPACES - not LOW-VALUES - and :352 moves 10 into WS-IDX, so the fill DESCENDS: ADMIN002 lands in row 10 and ADMIN001 in row 9, leaving rows 1 to 8 blank. A two-record backward page therefore sits at the BOTTOM of the screen, which is the exact inverse of a short forward page. The third READPREV inside the loop at :355 reports ENDFILE, so :668-674 sets end of file and paints 'You have reached the top of the page...' - and note that this is the IN-LOOP position of that arm, where case20 reaches the same arm from the look-behind at :363, the same pairing case03 and case18 make for READNEXT. Two consequences are preserved exactly as they are, and they are the point of this case (practice B5). First, POPULATE-USER-DATA never reaches WS-IDX 1, so the dual receiver at :389 never fires and CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST keeps its INCOMING value ADMIN003 - a stale boundary key naming a record that is no longer even on the page; only :435 fired, at row 10, so USRID-LAST is ADMIN002. Second, :362's guard is false because end of file was set inside the loop, so the whole :363-371 block is skipped: no look-behind READPREV, no SUBTRACT at :367 and no MOVE at :369, and CDEMO-CU00-PAGE-NUM passes through UNCHANGED at 2. That is the third of three mutually exclusive backward outcomes, against case07's SUBTRACT and case20's MOVE. :374 still issues the ENDBR and :376-377 writes that unchanged 2 into the page-number field and sends, and there is no MOVE SPACE TO USRIDINO on this path - the forward page has one at :328 - so the start-key field keeps whatever it showed, as do SEL0001 through SEL0010, which INITIALIZE-USER-DATA does not touch. The COBOL performs two SENDs here, at :674 and at :377, and both compose the same image; the published handler exposes one transmission, and that is the image pinned below. Provenance: statically derived by structured reading of the paragraph against app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy, app/cpy-bms/COUSR00.CPY and app/jcl/DUSRSECJ.jcl, and never captured from an execution of the legacy program (risk R-A). Declared gap, recorded rather than left silent: the :210-214 invalid-selection WHEN OTHER arm is driven by UserMenuControllerTest under gates G49 and G50 rather than by a parity case, because gate G15 fixes the budget at exactly twenty cases per program.",
